# PREDICTION for ROOT lane run 19, committed ALONE and BEFORE the run.
#
# STEP -1 of `scratch/lane-run-7-procedure.md`. The derivation is written out so it is
# checkable independently of whether the number matches — R19-06, R20-07 and D0A-R26-06 are
# three runs whose FIGURE was right and whose EXPLANATION was wrong.
#
# ORDERING IS CONVENTION, NOT MECHANISM (D0A-R22-01, reopened). Held for runs 13-18.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHY RUN 19 IS OWED, AND WHY IT IS DIFFERENT FROM THE LAST FIVE
#
# The D0A-R30 extraction gave the daemon's shutdown policy its first tests — closing a gap that
# had stood for three rounds, in which the code was compiled, linked, and run PAST rather than
# THROUGH. **Those tests have only ever run unprivileged.**
#
# That is the weakest possible lane for this particular subject. The policy exists because a
# ROOT daemon must reap children it cannot trust to exit; "it passed unprivileged" is evidence
# about the lane where the failure is cheapest. Two things found during the extraction make
# that concrete rather than rhetorical:
#
#   * `shutdown_child` guarded `pid <= 0` inside the REAPER and fell through to
#     `kill(Pid::from_raw(0), SIGKILL)` — signalling the whole process group. It SIGKILLed the
#     test runner (exit 137). A guard on the WAIT side is not a guard on the SIGNAL side.
#   * `a_pid_that_is_not_our_child` named **pid 1**. The kill is unreachable, so it passed —
#     but unprivileged a stray `kill(1, SIGKILL)` is EPERM and at ROOT it is init. Changed to
#     `pid_max` at `0cf555e`, BEFORE this run, because a test should not stake a machine on its
#     own correctness.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DERIVATION
#
# Base: run 18 measured EXECUTED 208 / SKIPPED 5 / reported 213.
#       Current unprivileged pair: EXECUTED 196 / SKIPPED 25 / reported 221 (measured
#       2026-09-07 at 0cf555e, re-measured by the pre-commit hook across all 17 targets).
#
# Delta since run 18: **EIGHT tests added**, all in the new `shutdown` module; none removed.
# Root-gating verified BY GREP of each body — no `geteuid`, no `SKIP` branch, no
# `bwrap_available`, no path-existence guard:
#
#   a_cooperating_child_is_reaped_within_grace_with_its_status_preserved   no gate
#   a_child_that_outlives_the_grace_period_is_killed_and_reaped            no gate
#   an_already_reaped_child_is_reported_gone_without_waiting               no gate
#   a_pid_that_is_not_our_child_terminates_the_policy_promptly             no gate
#   non_positive_pids_are_refused_rather_than_signalling_a_group           no gate
#   children_are_shut_down_independently_and_each_outcome_is_attributed    no gate
#   only_an_unreaped_child_counts_as_failed_cleanup                        no gate
#   the_daemon_delegates_shutdown_and_does_not_reap_by_hand                no gate
#
# So: 208 + 8 = 216 EXECUTED, skip set unchanged at 5, reported 221.
#   unprivileged  196 + 25 = 221
#   root          216 +  5 = 221
# Equal totals are NOT the evidence (D0A-R27-04); §4b's identity comparison is.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE TWO THINGS TO READ FOR — AND WHAT EACH CAN ACTUALLY SHOW
#
# **1. THE DELEGATION GUARD CANNOT DIFFER BY LANE, AND SAYING SO IS THE HONEST ANSWER.**
#
# `the_daemon_delegates_shutdown_and_does_not_reap_by_hand` uses `include_str!` — it reads
# `bin/delphi-runtimed.rs` AT COMPILE TIME and asserts on its text. **It executes no process and
# touches no privilege.** Running it as root re-checks a string that was already checked, so a
# green at root adds NOTHING to what the unprivileged run established.
#
# What it does establish, in either lane, is real: `main` calls `shutdown_all` and carries no
# second copy of the policy. It caught one — `ChildReaper::Drop` — on its first run.
#
# What NOTHING in run 19 establishes is that the daemon's `main` BRANCH is taken at root after a
# terminal outcome. That is ASSEMBLY coverage, it is owed, and the reviewer named it separately.
# The only root exercise of that binary, `b1_daemon_binary_runs_the_assembled_flow`, still
# SKIPS. **Do not read a green delegation guard as evidence about the root call site.**
#
# **2. THE PER-CHILD ATTRIBUTION CASES ARE PREDICTED TO PASS IDENTICALLY — AND IDENTICAL IS NOT
# COVERED.**
#
# `children_are_shut_down_independently_and_each_outcome_is_attributed` spawns its own children
# (`sh -c exit 0` and `sleep 120`) and reaps them. **Reaping and signalling your own children
# requires no privilege**, so root should behave exactly as unprivileged, and the prediction is
# that both children report the same outcomes in both lanes.
#
# If that holds, the correct record is that the lanes were **IDENTICAL**, not that root
# **COVERED** anything the unprivileged run did not. Root's extra power is over processes that
# are NOT its children — which is precisely the case this test does not construct, and precisely
# the case where the pid-1 fixture would have mattered.
#
# **A DIFFERENCE HERE WOULD BE A RESULT**, and worth stopping for: it would mean the policy's
# behaviour depends on privilege in a way nothing predicted.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT A GREEN RUN 19 WILL NOT ESTABLISH
#
# 1. Assembly coverage of the daemon's exit path (above) — owed.
# 2. R29-05's unreaped-child branch: still needs a child in uninterruptible sleep, which nothing
#    constructs. `Unreaped` is asserted only through `only_an_unreaped_child_counts_as_failed_cleanup`,
#    which constructs the VALUE, not the CONDITION.
# 3. R29-06's EINTR retry: still needs a signal inside the `waitpid` window; nothing delivers one.
# 4. The mutation campaign remains unprivileged-only; the five root-gated tests have never been
#    mutation-tested.
# 5. The suspend divergence is unmeasured; `action.timeout` is enforced nowhere (R9-04).
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TIMING TOLERANCES — two are NEW this run
#
#   a_child_that_outlives_the_grace_period_...   150 ms grace, 3 s post-kill, asserts the whole
#                                                shutdown completes in < 5 s. Under load the
#                                                grace expires SOONER, so the margin is in the
#                                                safe direction.
#   an_already_reaped_child_...                  asserts < 1 s. The tightest new bound.
#   a_pid_that_is_not_our_child_...              asserts < 2 s.
#   plus the carried wire deadline tests and boot_secs' 1 s sampling gap.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A MISMATCH IS A RESULT. Record which side was wrong. Do not adjust this derivation until it
# agrees with the measurement.

EXPECTED_EXECUTED=216
EXPECTED_SKIPPED=5
EXPECTED_REPORTED=221
